  "body": "Delivered the complete independent ACVC longer-C B01 scientific review for the fixed task at 11da57fca73effbee96979dce0dd40568600ea12:\n\nhttps://github.com/CartmanFatass/My-paper-code/blob/fcd806cb2b1f99158540d8f7d1123a9df249b214/docs/research/candidates/acvc/pro_packets/20260914_cluster_longer_c_b01_scientific_review/archive/RESPONSE.md\n\nThe review identifies no result-invalidating defect in the supplied record and confirms that the earlier workload-reporting finding is resolved. It preserves the separate UP readings, useful own-dwell, all adverse worlds, and the changed-exposure single-programme claim ceiling. Its next-measurement preference is a genuinely new paired-exposure B, with explicit checkpoint dependence and endpoint-versus-change distinctions; it also addresses the stronger fixed-recipe population alternative and report/retention tradeoff. These are scientific recommendations, not experiment selection, funding or a lifecycle verdict.\n\nEvidence retains the task's exact per-path commits: 45955bdf7026769f703ae580caf814fdc1655421 for scientific records, 914a3d0e78d49d385c54aaec0776ead63712b624 for inspected source, and f238712bc28cd1d9bc81c853f67cd500eaa8b202 for methods. The verified delivery commit adds only the specified response file. No source, card, prior response, main or scientific state was changed; no code execution, experiment or outcome reanalysis occurred. DM responds and owns ordinary research choices; Portfolio retains final direction lifecycle.",
